p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids May to June came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them, the most of any pair. In 2025, on the middle of the grids, March to April hit 48% and October to November 50%. So far in 2026, on that same middle, March to April sits at 50% and April to May at 63%. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, grid 20298 at 62%.</p>"}
